      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RISING FAME (10) sets the standard after holding on well for eighth at Belmont Park, beaten three and a half lengths in CL1 grade after leading to the turn. She was again respected in betting there, has a solid 1300m profile with one win and five placings at the trip, and looks the most dependable race-fit option. KAZANA (7) is less convincing on recent finishing positions, having ended last campaign with two plain runs, but she has won at her only attempt around 1300m and the apprentice claim helps her return. ADMIRE THE GIRL (4) has stronger claims than the form line reads after being held up near the 100m at Bunbury, and her previous wide run at Belmont Park is easy enough to overlook in this grade. WHO SAZ YES (8) was only beaten a length and a half at Pinjarra despite covering ground from the 800m, and her record at this track keeps her in the minor-money discussion.",
